      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "llm are forgetful and for that we need to add memory module to them and this is\none of important module to add to llm toward making an agent, as we can see\nfrom the image above, the llm have this forgetful behavior, the llm you mostly\ninteract with like chatgpt, claude have memory module tools etc added to them\nand therefore we need to add memory to owr model.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "llm are forgetful and for that we need to add memory module to them and this is one of important module to add to llm toward making an agent, as we can see from the image above, the llm have this forgetful behavior, the llm you mostly interact with like chatgpt, claude have memory module tools etc added to them and therefore we need to add memory to owr model.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Fu_rX_zCannVHlXPB_0ue",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 241.265625,
      "y": 499.28125,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1665862946,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 24276002,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793265321530,
      "created": 1793265309623,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Memory for LLMs tends to follow human memory types, as the agents that we\nattempt to create are often modeled after human behavior. Instead of going\nthrough all forms of human memory types, of which there are many, the “Cognitive\nArchitectures for Language Agents” paper describes four types of external\nmemory that we often see in agents, working memory for short-term use, and\nthree variants of long-term memory: episodic, semantic, and procedural memory.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Memory for LLMs tends to follow human memory types, as the agents that we attempt to create are often modeled after human behavior. Instead of going through all forms of human memory types, of which there are many, the “Cognitive Architectures for Language Agents” paper describes four types of external memory that we often see in agents, working memory for short-term use, and three variants of long-term memory: episodic, semantic, and procedural memory.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uihzh-jrR8coKlrTAJwO7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 254.265625,
      "y": 661.28125,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1817143970,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 386574882,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793265463677,
      "created": 1793265462263,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "For long-term memory, there are three forms described:\n\nEpisodic memory\n\n    Involves remembering specific events and experiences from one’s past (e.g.,\nyour last birthday party). For agents, this typically involves specific actions the\nagent has taken thus far and their outcomes.\nSemantic memory\n\n    Involves remembering knowledge about the world (e.g., the capital of France).\nFor agents, this may involve querying an external database like Wikipedia or the\ncodebase that you’re working on.\nProcedural memory\n\n    Involves remembering patterns of how to do things (e.g., writing code in\nPython). For agents, this can be information hidden in its parameters (also called\nparametric memory) or the system prompt, which persists across calls.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "For long-term memory, there are three forms described:\n\nEpisodic memory\n\n    Involves remembering specific events and experiences from one’s past (e.g., your last birthday party). For agents, this typically involves specific actions the agent has taken thus far and their outcomes.\nSemantic memory\n\n    Involves remembering knowledge about the world (e.g., the capital of France). For agents, this may involve querying an external database like Wikipedia or the codebase that you’re working on.\nProcedural memory\n\n    Involves remembering patterns of how to do things (e.g., writing code in Python). For agents, this can be information hidden in its parameters (also called parametric memory) or the system prompt, which persists across calls.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
