      "updated": 1793269551865,
      "created": 1793268618060,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "this approach works but there is  a shortcoming  , our model has a limited\ncontext window, and for that we need a way to make sure our answers are nto\ncut short and there are sevel techniques to deal with this , one of them is\ntrimming., another strategy is summarization,",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "this approach works but there is  a shortcoming  , our model has a limited context window, and for that we need a way to make sure our answers are nto cut short and there are sevel techniques to deal with this , one of them is trimming., another strategy is summarization,",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lW2BiIQB4S4NbT7EUmZGF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 261.265625,
      "y": 2219.78125,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ae",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1125352510,
      "version": 115,
      "versionNonce": 1969611106,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793269547592,
      "created": 1793269533640,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "As the conversation history and the number of actions that an agent has taken\ngrows, so does the need for long-term memory. However, its usefulness is not\nlimited to conversation history but may also include proprietary or external\nknowledge. Long-term memory typically involves maintaining one or more external\ndatabases that can be queried to extract additional information. This can\ncontain information about previous traces or states of the agent (episodic\nmemory) or information unrelated to the agent’s behavior but about the context\nof your application instead (semantic memory), like your organization’s documents",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "As the conversation history and the number of actions that an agent has taken grows, so does the need for long-term memory. However, its usefulness is not limited to conversation history but may also include proprietary or external knowledge. Long-term memory typically involves maintaining one or more external databases that can be queried to extract additional information. This can contain information about previous traces or states of the agent (episodic memory) or information unrelated to the agent’s behavior but about the context of your application instead (semantic memory), like your organization’s documents",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "T38hoiciTF7IQumkvkKBW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 265.265625,
      "y": 2414.28125,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "af",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 570740578,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 958640802,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793269695106,
      "created": 1793269688045,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Arguably, the most common method for giving your agent, or any LLM for that\nmatter, long-term memory is Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). RAG typically\nconsists of two stages: ingestion and inference.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Arguably, the most common method for giving your agent, or any LLM for that matter, long-term memory is Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). RAG typically consists of two stages: ingestion and inference.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3JUsviUxENkY135tkCos4",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 268.9502611185985,
      "y": 2508.6500089158344,
      "width": 727.9487870619955,
      "height": 192.63124108416574,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "transparent",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ag",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1024351714,
      "version": 259,
      "versionNonce": 1673042914,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793269789675,
      "created": 1793269775269,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "status": "saved",
